desc: Cut to the Chase Beat Slicer (LiveCut Enhanced port) by chmaha
tags: slicer beat-slicer stutter glitch bbcut livecut modulation
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Live beat slicer. It records the incoming audio in tempo-synced chunks and plays it back cut up:
  repeats, stutters, rolls and fills, with random level, pan and pitch per cut, an optional bit
  crusher and a comb filter that follow the cuts. It locks to the project tempo and position; when
  the transport is stopped it keeps cutting on its own clock.
  Three cutting styles: CutProc11 (repeats with an end-of-phrase stutter), WarpCut (accelerating and
  slowing rolls) and SQPusher (Squarepusher-style fills). Seed picks a repeatable random pattern.
  The Modulation page has 4 LFOs, 4 Wander sources (smooth random drift), and a 16-slot matrix that
  routes them, the mod wheel, velocity, aftertouch or the input level to almost every control.
  Ported from LiveCut Enhanced https://github.com/dadda123/LiveCut-enhanced (the fork's loop-wrap fix
  included) with the modulation system from its pull request #1 by Xenodimensional. LiveCut is Remy
  Muller's (mdsp) Livecut, based on the BBCut algorithm by Nick Collins.
  The random generator follows the Windows build of the original, so a Seed gives the same cuts there.
  Original code GPL-2.0-or-later
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
